        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Fuzzy Match CSV Data"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1779446976559"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 5738,
            "y": 12754
          },
          "code": "FUZZY_MATCH_CSV_DATA",
          "id": "1771302701325",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1771302701327_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are matching source data attributes to target CSV attributes for Oracle HSDL load preparation.\n\nSOURCE_HEADERS_JSON:\n{{$context.$nodes.PREPARE_FUZZY_MATCH_INPUTS.$output.result.sourceHeaders}}\n\nTARGET_HEADERS_JSON:\n{{$context.$nodes.PREPARE_FUZZY_MATCH_INPUTS.$output.result.targetHeaders}}\n\nTask:\n- For every target header, choose the best matching source header from SOURCE_HEADERS_JSON, or use null when no good match exists.\n- Use all source headers as candidates for matching.\n- Return exactly one mapping object for every target header, in the same order as TARGET_HEADERS_JSON.\n- The targetHeader value must be copied exactly from TARGET_HEADERS_JSON.\n- The sourceHeader value must be copied exactly from SOURCE_HEADERS_JSON, or null.\n- Do not rename, remove, add, trim, normalize, or reorder target headers.\n- Do not add source-only columns.\n- Do not generate CSV.\n\nMatching guidance:\n- Prefer exact and case-insensitive matches.\n- Use semantic similarity where needed, because header names can use business prefixes or slightly different phrasing.\n- Object-prefixed targets like Job_ActiveStatus, Job_JobCode, and Job_ManagerLevel should map to ActiveStatus, JobCode, and ManagerLevel when those source headers exist.\n- Avoid weak matches based only on generic words such as id, code, name, type, date, status, or flag.\n- If a target header has no reliable source match, set sourceHeader to null.\n\nOutput format:\nReturn only a JSON object matching this shape:\n{\"mappings\":[{\"targetHeader\":\"<exact target header>\",\"sourceHeader\":\"<exact source header or null>\",\"confidenceReason\":\"<short reason>\"}]}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Convert output CSV to base64",
            "returnType": "string",
            "sourceCode": "const generatedCsvOutput = $context.$nodes.GENERATE_MATCHED_CSV_DATA.$output;\nconst csvText =\n  (generatedCsvOutput && generatedCsvOutput.result != null\n    ? generatedCsvOutput.result\n    : generatedCsvOutput) + \"\";\n\nif (typeof btoa !== \"function\") {\n  throw new Error(\n    \"Native btoa is not available in this Code node runtime; cannot base64 encode large CSV without exceeding the statement limit.\"\n  );\n}\n\nlet result = \"\";\ntry {\n  result = btoa(csvText);\n} catch (error) {\n  throw new Error(\n    \"Failed to base64 encode generated CSV with native btoa. Ensure the generated CSV is ASCII/Latin-1 compatible. \" +\n      (error && error.message ? error.message : \"\")\n  );\n}\n\nreturn result;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1771303942217"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 5732,
            "y": 13198
          },
          "code": "CONVERT_OUTPUT_CSV_TO_BASE64",
